---
name: dev-sanity-task
version: 2.17.1
description: lead sanity check assignment for the member that fills the dev-sanity role (resolve-role dev-sanity). task_id is the sanity check bead. The member splits the checked bead per numbered deliverable (sanity-split), runs LLM and JEV checkers per deliverable and a selected merge with lint alongside, then reports PASS or FAIL. Not QA.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - checked_bead
  - sprint
  - worktree_path
  - branch
  - commit
  - base
  - pr_number
  - pr_url
  - primary_checkout
  - lint_command
optional_variables:
  - layer_prs
defaults:
  layer_prs: []
metadata:
  type: dev-sanity-task
  tags:
    - stage:dev-sanity
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: dev-sanity-start
    stage: dev-sanity
    transition: start
---
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" mode="dev-sanity">
  <description><![CDATA[Sanity check `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`: each numbered deliverable is written; lint passes. This is not QA.]]></description>

  <checked-bead><![CDATA[{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}]]></checked-bead>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <base><![CDATA[{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}]]></base>
  <layer-prs><![CDATA[{{ layer_prs | join(" ") | string | cdata_escape }}]]></layer-prs>
  <pr number="{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}"><![CDATA[{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}]]></pr>
  <lint-command><![CDATA[{{ lint_command | string | cdata_escape }}]]></lint-command>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Before any claim, run `bd ready -n 0 --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} 'any(.[]; .id == $b)'`; when it prints `false` follow a1. Run `test -n "{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}" && test -n "{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}"` or refuse `SANITY.PR_REQUIRED`. Run `gh pr view {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} --json baseRefName,headRefName,headRefOid --jq '.baseRefName + " " + .headRefName + " " + .headRefOid'`; require, else `SANITY.NOT_STACKED`: base `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` and head `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`; `gh api 'repos/{owner}/{repo}/stacks' --paginate --jq '.[]'` (GitHub's stacks, never local `gh stack` tracking) has an open stack whose `pull_requests` include {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} with `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` the `head.ref` of the open PR before it (the stack's `base.ref` for its first open PR), or, in no open stack, the PR is layer 0 awaiting layer 1: `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` is `<pr_target>` below and `gh pr list --head {{ base | string | cdata_escape }} --state open --json headRefName` prints `[]`; then `git fetch origin`; unless `<pr_target>` = `bd show {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq -r '.[0].metadata.pr_target'` (a lower bound; a poured dev bead uses its `metadata.sprint_bead`'s; none skips this check) is `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}`, `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/<pr_target> origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` exits 0 (a `<pr_target>` gone from origin passes when a PR in `gh pr list --head <pr_target> --state merged --json mergeCommit` has its merge commit in `origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}`). Run `git log --format=%H origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}..{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }} | grep -q .` or refuse `SANITY.ZERO_DELTA`; `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }} {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}` or refuse `SANITY.NOT_REBASED`; `test -z "$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no | grep -v -e ' \.beads\.gate\.lock$' -e ' \.sc-compose/')"` or refuse `SANITY.DIRTY_TREE` (ignored paths: `IGNORED_STATUS_PATHS` in `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/assignment-gates.py`); `bd history {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq -e 'any(.[]; .Issue.status == "closed" and (.Issue.close_reason // "" | startswith("PASS at ")))'` and refuse `SANITY_FROZEN` when it prints `true` (a snapshot closed with reason `PASS at <sha>`; a note or other reason mentioning PASS does not count). These codes are only for mismatches: a command that fails to run (`gh`, `git fetch`, `bd`: a nonzero exit or error, not an answer) refuses `GATE_CANNOT_RUN`, a serious failure announced as in `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md` Lead Role. Reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal; if none matches, report the signature to the task assigner for classification and cite that message instead. Do not create a per-task shadow bead or delay the refusal. Otherwise claim and start the check.]]></step>
    <step id="a1"><![CDATA[If it prints `false`, the bead is not ready: do not claim it or start the task. Find the root cause: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` (status, assignee), `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'` (normally `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` still open), and `bd show <blocker>` for each. Then refuse; never wait: close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`, `bead_state` `open`, `reason_md` naming the bead, why it is not ready, which bead or agent must move, and, for a blocker not yet its dependency, the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`, so `bd ready` lists the bead only once the blocker closes. The task assigner re-assigns it then.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Follow `.claude/agents/dev-sanity.md`, the canonical coordinator. Run sanity-split once, with `--layer-pr <n>` for each PR in `<layer-prs>` (empty: the single range from `<base>`), and send identical assignments to both reviewers concurrently. Keep both raw result arrays. When a reviewer's last reply or timeout envelope arrives, record its completion epoch before merging or waiting for shared lint, then merge it immediately with `--started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch>`. Append no history until selected merge sets the final verdict. Build one strict selection array, one entry per deliverable; record the selected start epoch when selection begins and completion epoch when `selection.json` is written. Invoke selected merge only as `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-merge ... --reviewer sanity-selected --started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch> --llm-vars <sanity-llm-vars.json> --jev-vars <sanity-jev-vars.json> --selection <selection.json>`; it ignores stdin. Append history in exact order `sanity-llm`, then `sanity-jev`, both rows with the selected verdict as `--final-verdict`; if selection or selected merge cannot run, use `CANNOT_RUN` and still append LLM/JEV. Copy only the `sanity-selected` vars to `<scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json` for steps e/e1. Exit 4: wait for shared lint; retries reuse supplied epochs. Selected cannot-run routes to e2.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[PASS: For each `checker_defect`, append the selection entry to the matching workflow class bead (or report it to the task assigner) and cite it in notes. Then close the bead and task together: first `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "PASS at <sha>"`; only if it succeeded, `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/dev-sanity-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json` with `verdict` PASS. Closing the bead releases every dev bead that required `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}`.]]></step>
    <step id="e1"><![CDATA[Selected FAIL only. Keep the sanity bead **open**; closing it would release dependent dev beads. Preserve every finding unchanged. For each `checker_defect`, append the selection entry to the matching workflow class bead (or report it to the task assigner) and cite it in notes; checker defects create no child (the selection record and workflow-issue class bead carry their evidence). Do not otherwise edit the checked parent. Before closing this task, run this exact command against the merge-created vars file; it creates one open `bug` child per finding under `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}`, copies the report fields verbatim to child metadata and description, and adds each declared inter-finding blocking edge; with `--reviewer sc-sanity-selected`, each child records the selected LLM/JEV source:

```bash
{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-create-findings \
  --task {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --bead {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} \
  --vars <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json \
  --reviewer sc-sanity-selected \
  --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY" > <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-finding-children.json
```

The script never creates a finding-sanity gate or adds an edge to another planned sprint: the phase's plan file is the minimum set of sprint-to-sprint dependencies, and only the lead adds one (including one discovered in motion); recommend it in the report instead.

The script gives each blocking child priority `clamp(parent priority - 1, P1, P4)` and the parent's required difficulty. The parent/child hierarchy is the parent closure gate: `bd` rejects a parent-to-child `blocks` edge because it would deadlock the child. For each report `depends_on` selector, the script creates `<dependent-finding-child> --blocks--> <prerequisite-finding-child>`, so the dependent fix cannot close first. It adds the ordered `finding_bead_ids` array to the same vars file used by `atm task close`, so the final report links every child; do not write those ids to parent notes (the graph is authoritative). A failure to create or wire every child is cannot-run, not a completed FAIL. After the script: reopen the checked bead with `bd reopen {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "sanity FAIL at <sha>: <n> findings" --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY"` (this sanity bead's `blocks` edge re-blocks it); return the sanity bead to the queue with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "FAIL at <sha>: <n> findings"`; then close the task with the same `atm task close … completed` command and `verdict` FAIL. The task assigner reviews the children and assigns the dev fix; the lead may overrule, amend, split, or reassign children. The parent cannot close until all children close; only then may final parent closure occur, readying the next sanity run.]]></step>
    <step id="e2"><![CDATA[If the selected check cannot run (plan not splittable, worktree missing, commit not pushed, a check timed out or was rejected twice), reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite its class id in the refusal; if none matches, report the signature to the task assigner for classification and cite that message. Do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. Return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "<code>; workflow class or escalation <reference>: <reason>"`, then close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. A blocker is not a failure: when a prerequisite reopens or the work needs an unlanded fix, stop, return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why>"`, then close the task `refused` as above (`bead_state` `open`), its `reason_md` naming the blocker and the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never stay active waiting.]]></step>
    <step id="e3"><![CDATA[After the close, render the console table as the canonical coordinator specifies (`tail -n 20` of the phase ledger through `jq -s '{runs: .}'` into `templates/sanity-run-table.md.j2`) and include it in the user-visible completion reply before reading ATM again. If the ledger or render fails, report `SANITY.STATUS_TABLE_UNAVAILABLE` and the error; no verdict changes. Pre-dispatch refusals have no reviewer row.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[After the close and the required user-visible completion reply in step e3 (whenever reviewer results exist), read ATM again.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
